# Simple Limb Sketch Diagram

```
    Shoulder Joint (3 DOF)
         |
         | Upper Arm
         |
    Elbow Joint (1 DOF)
         |
         | Forearm
         |
    Wrist Joint (3 DOF)
         |
       Hand/End-Effector
```

## Description

This diagram illustrates the basic kinematic structure of a humanoid robot arm with multiple degrees of freedom (DOF). The shoulder provides 3 degrees of freedom (rotation in 3 planes), the elbow provides 1 degree of freedom (flexion/extension), and the wrist provides 3 degrees of freedom (rotation and articulation). This configuration allows the arm to reach various positions and orientations in 3D space while maintaining dexterity for manipulation tasks.